{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 450,
    "dDurationMs": 5179,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "News of the Chinese Long March 5 rocket burning up on re-entry has made waves through the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5629,
    "dDurationMs": 6590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "world- in some cases, quite literally, as the debris from the rocket burned up over Saudi Arabia"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 12219,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and splashed down in the Indian Ocean near the Maldives."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 15999,
    "dDurationMs": 4161,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while it made a lot of people very nervous to know a 22 ton rocket was going to fall"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 20160,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "out the sky, this sort of thing happens all the time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 23740,
    "dDurationMs": 4670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Boosters, dead satellites, and sometimes even old space stations get dropped out of the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28410,
    "dDurationMs": 1730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sky fairly often."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 30140,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "While the litter seems a little inconsiderate,\nthis is probably far safer than the alternative:"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 35570,
    "dDurationMs": 2340,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "leaving junk in orbit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 37910,
    "dDurationMs": 5260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Just last month a hole was found in a robotic arm on the international space station - punctured"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43170,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "clean through by a fast-moving piece of shrapnel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 46310,
    "dDurationMs": 7590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The accumulation of space junk poses a huge risk to all human operations in space especially"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 53900,
    "dDurationMs": 5249,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "if we cross the threshold into the chain reaction of exponentially growing collisions known"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 59149,
    "dDurationMs": 2088,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as Kessler Syndrome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 66251,
    "dDurationMs": 5048,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The launch of Sputnik in 1957 kicked off a\nspace race, and the number of satellites in"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 71299,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space has grown ever since, and in recent\nyears it’s really taken off like a rocket."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 76729,
    "dDurationMs": 4121,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "There are more than 3300 operational satellites\nbuzzing around up there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 80850,
    "dDurationMs": 1499,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But they aren’t alone."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 82349,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They orbit in the midst of a giant cloud of\ndebris - rocket boosters, protective shields,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87229,
    "dDurationMs": 4511,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "old broken satellites and more, around 10,000 objects that are large enough to be tracked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 91740,
    "dDurationMs": 1229,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by radar."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92969,
    "dDurationMs": 3451,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are uncontrolled and they are moving\nvery, very fast."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 96420,
    "dDurationMs": 4089,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The quickest low-altitude orbits circle the\nEarth 16 times a day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 100509,
    "dDurationMs": 5170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A collision with one of these means instant\nobliteration into countless shards."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 105679,
    "dDurationMs": 7082,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And speaking of shards, there may be over 100 million pieces of debris so small they can’t be tracked"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 112761,
    "dDurationMs": 6408,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And while a loose screw or paint chip may not be all that scary on earth, at orbital speeds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119169,
    "dDurationMs": 4981,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 7 km/s they can carry as much energy as a cannonball."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 124150,
    "dDurationMs": 5539,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Right now there are probably over 3 million\nkilograms of space junk, vastly outweighing"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 129689,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our operational satellites and nearby natural meteoroids combined."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 134509,
    "dDurationMs": 4251,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- forming a giant space-tornado of death above our heads."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 138760,
    "dDurationMs": 4949,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The main thing protecting satellites from\nspace junk is space itself."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 143709,
    "dDurationMs": 6390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Space is, as the name implies, spacious, and so collisions are relatively rare, or at least"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 150099,
    "dDurationMs": 1521,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for the moment they're rare."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 151620,
    "dDurationMs": 6259,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But as the number of satellites increases,\nthe risk of collisions also increases."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 157879,
    "dDurationMs": 4101,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And collisions produce more space junk that produces more collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161980,
    "dDurationMs": 5009,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This sort of collision cascade is known as\nthe Kessler Syndrome, after Donald Kessler"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 166989,
    "dDurationMs": 3131,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "who pointed out the danger in 1978."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 170120,
    "dDurationMs": 5449,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The movie Gravity depicted this domino-chain of destruction as unfolding over minutes to"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 175569,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "hours."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 176569,
    "dDurationMs": 2761,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s not how it would actually play out."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 179330,
    "dDurationMs": 6610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact the Kessler Syndrome is already playing out - albeit a lot more slowly."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185940,
    "dDurationMs": 1969,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it may soon speed up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187909,
    "dDurationMs": 5321,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "To understand the risk we face, let’s think\na bit about exponential processes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 193230,
    "dDurationMs": 5410,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Kessler Syndrome is due to what we call a positive feedback cycle - that’s any process"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198640,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "whose outcome tends to increase the rate of the process, leading to exponential increase."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 203720,
    "dDurationMs": 3629,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The more space junk we have, the more space junk we make."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 207349,
    "dDurationMs": 6021,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But a positive feedback process can be prevented from entering that exponential mode if it’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 213370,
    "dDurationMs": 1560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "suppressed in some way."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 214930,
    "dDurationMs": 5750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In the case of satellite collisions, exponential increase is inevitable unless debris is removed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 220680,
    "dDurationMs": 3990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "from orbit or the risk of collision is mitigated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 224670,
    "dDurationMs": 4939,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And that needs to happen faster and better\nthan the rate that space junk is made."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229609,
    "dDurationMs": 2671,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s talk about mitigation first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232280,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Large pieces of space junk can be tracked\nusing ground based radar and more precise"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 237170,
    "dDurationMs": 2679,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "optical and lidar methods."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 239849,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And their future trajectories can be calculated to predict possible future collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 245239,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A functional satellite in harm's way can then steer itself into a safe orbit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 250629,
    "dDurationMs": 4590,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The international space station has to dodge tracked space junk roughly once a year."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255219,
    "dDurationMs": 2591,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But this method is far from perfect."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 257810,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Below around 1000 km, Earth’s atmosphere is incredibly diffuse but still present."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264290,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It produces a drag that causes orbits to slowly decay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 268040,
    "dDurationMs": 3050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s ultimately a good thing, as I’ll\nshow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 271090,
    "dDurationMs": 5199,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it also means we can lose track of space junk because the amount of drag can change"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 276289,
    "dDurationMs": 6471,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "- in particular, during times of high solar activity when more energy is pumped into the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282760,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "atmosphere, causing it to puff up and cause increased drag to higher altitudes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 287950,
    "dDurationMs": 4570,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The smaller the space junk the more susceptible it is to atmospheric drag."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 292520,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That gives us a sweet spot for ‘lethal’\ndebris - pieces of junk in the size range"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 298060,
    "dDurationMs": 5870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of 1 to 10 cm are the hardest to track, and\nalmost impossible to keep track of."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 303930,
    "dDurationMs": 5680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And yet are still large enough to cause ‘lethal’ collisions- the kind that can obliterate a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309610,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "satellite if they hit right in the main body."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 312630,
    "dDurationMs": 4790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And there are something like half a million\nof these hyper-velocity space bullets flitting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 317420,
    "dDurationMs": 1230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "around up there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 318650,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Improved tracking facilities can help here - better, faster observations will help us"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323110,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "survive this game of cosmic dodgeball a little longer."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 326970,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But tracking only goes so far."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 329640,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Junk smaller than around a centimeter can’t be tracked at all - your paint flecks and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 333800,
    "dDurationMs": 3460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "rocket exhaust and shards from prior collisions."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 337260,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The only way this stuff gets cleaned up is\nif its orbit decays."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 341010,
    "dDurationMs": 5030,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I already mentioned that orbits decay due\nto interaction with the upper reaches of Earth’s"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 346040,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "atmosphere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 347040,
    "dDurationMs": 4490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Below around 1000 km, that drag slows satellites, causing them to fall into lower orbits where"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 351530,
    "dDurationMs": 2020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the drag is even greater."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 353550,
    "dDurationMs": 5710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is another positive feedback loop - orbital decay accelerates until the satellite finally"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 359260,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "burns in a glorious blaze of re-entry."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 363000,
    "dDurationMs": 5960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Satellites in low earth orbit may need to\nbe boosted a few times a year to prevent this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 368960,
    "dDurationMs": 1580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "inspiral."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 370540,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "During a maximum of solar activity when our atmosphere extends further out, the lowest"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 374990,
    "dDurationMs": 3100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "satellites need to be boosted every 2-3 weeks."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378090,
    "dDurationMs": 5740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s annoying, but orbital decay is the\nmost important process for cleaning low-earth"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383830,
    "dDurationMs": 2970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orbit of defunct satellites and debris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 386800,
    "dDurationMs": 6480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Ultimately, the Kessler Syndrome can be avoided if orbital decay cleans up low-earth orbit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 393280,
    "dDurationMs": 3510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "faster than new launches and new collisions fill it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 396790,
    "dDurationMs": 5290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OK, let’s look a bit harder at the sources\nof space junk to see if these mitigating processes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 402080,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "have any hope of saving us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 403960,
    "dDurationMs": 6490,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Over 40% of the catalogued space junk is debris from the upper stages of a handful of US rockets"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 410450,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that exploded after releasing their payloads."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 413780,
    "dDurationMs": 4450,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These plus few other catastrophic events are responsible for most of the fragmentary space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 418230,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "junk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 419230,
    "dDurationMs": 5370,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Notably we have the 2009 collision between the Iridium 33 communication satellite and"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 424600,
    "dDurationMs": 5200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Kosmos 2251, a deactivated Soviet military satellite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 429800,
    "dDurationMs": 8180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "With a collision velocity of 11.6km/s, it\nwas less a smash than a splash, creating hundreds"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 437980,
    "dDurationMs": 5720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of fragments large enough to destroy other\nsatellites, and 10s of thousands of that could"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 443700,
    "dDurationMs": 2640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "cause damage or deactivate satellites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 446340,
    "dDurationMs": 3950,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Relatively few events have produced as much of our most dangerous space junk."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450290,
    "dDurationMs": 5470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, we have the times that nations deliberately destroyed their own satellites."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455760,
    "dDurationMs": 6470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US did this in 1985 with an air-to-space missile, and China demonstrated their capability"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 462230,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in 2007 with a ground-launched “kinetic\nkill vehicle”."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 466070,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The US followed a year later with operation\nburnt frost, ostensibly to eliminate the risk"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 471200,
    "dDurationMs": 6140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of reentry of a tank of toxic hydrazine - and\nthe reentry of that stuff would have been"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 477340,
    "dDurationMs": 1310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "very bad."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 478650,
    "dDurationMs": 3640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the timing after the Chinese launch does make you wonder."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 482290,
    "dDurationMs": 4230,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The issue with destroying satellites is that\nthe fragments don’t stay in the same orbit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 486520,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the progenitor satellite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 488740,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They quickly smear out in a ring around the\nEarth, making tracking and avoidance that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 492960,
    "dDurationMs": 1310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "much more difficult."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 494270,
    "dDurationMs": 6470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "John Gabbard, who was working at NORAD tracking missile test debris in 1960, noticed that"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 500740,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "debris also spreads out up and down."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503820,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This increases the altitude range of the risk, and can also mean that collisions in fast-decaying"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 509340,
    "dDurationMs": 3790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "orbits can still generate long-lasting debris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 513130,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So bringing  this all together we can paint a picture of our trashed orbital space."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 517940,
    "dDurationMs": 5840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Each collision tends to populate a wide swath of low-earth-orbit with dangerous debris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 523780,
    "dDurationMs": 2190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That debris then decays in orbit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 525970,
    "dDurationMs": 3750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Very slowly for the highest orbits, quite\nquickly for the lowest."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 529720,
    "dDurationMs": 5190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But those lowest orbits are continuously repopulated as debris rains down from higher up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 534910,
    "dDurationMs": 4170,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For example, even though the International\nSpace Station orbits several hundred kilometers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 539080,
    "dDurationMs": 5710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "below where the Iridium-Kosmos collision happened, on multiple occasions it's had to perform"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 544790,
    "dDurationMs": 5500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "collision avoidance maneuvers to avoid debris that’s sinking through its orbit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 550290,
    "dDurationMs": 5970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "As long as the self-cleaning of the lowest orbits outpaces the introduction of new debris,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 556260,
    "dDurationMs": 2050,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "we avoid exponential buildup."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 558310,
    "dDurationMs": 5390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But these lowest orbits are the most useful\nand cheapest to launch to - and so are the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 563700,
    "dDurationMs": 1360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "most densely populated."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 565060,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Add to that the rain of debris from above,\nand these are the most at risk of the Kessler"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 570440,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Syndrome."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 571560,
    "dDurationMs": 3150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So how long until the collision cascade?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 574710,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Actually, it’s already happening."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 577390,
    "dDurationMs": 2710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "More debris is produced than is removed."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 580100,
    "dDurationMs": 3700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Exponential buildup doesn’t have to happen over the course of a 90 minute Hollywood movie"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 583800,
    "dDurationMs": 1980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to be dangerous."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 585780,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In 1978, Donald Kessler estimated that the\nfirst satellite collision would probably happen"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 590720,
    "dDurationMs": 4910,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "some time in the next two to three decades, which was pretty spot on with the Iridium-Kosmos"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 595630,
    "dDurationMs": 2580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "destruction just over a decade ago."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 598210,
    "dDurationMs": 4990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the time to the next collision should\nbe shorter - and indeed there have been several"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 603200,
    "dDurationMs": 3730,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now, although thankfully none as cataclysmic as the first."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 606930,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’re currently in the slow part of the\nexponential rise, so we have years or decades"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 612230,
    "dDurationMs": 2790,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of useful space ahead of us."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 615020,
    "dDurationMs": 3240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But that can change if we change our launching habits for the worse."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 618260,
    "dDurationMs": 4710,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is where StarLink deserves a mention."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 622970,
    "dDurationMs": 6430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "SpaceX plans to launch constellation of over\n40,000 satellites as a global internet network."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 629400,
    "dDurationMs": 4650,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This will increase the number of satellites\nin orbit by a factor of more than 10."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 634050,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now SpaceX insists that they have collision mitigation systems planned, even if they haven’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 639430,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "told us exactly what those are."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 641470,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But even the best collision dodger can’t\ndo much against an untracked and untrackable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 645850,
    "dDurationMs": 1700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "shard of debris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 647550,
    "dDurationMs": 4750,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One hit can turn your agile, debris-dodging\nninja satellite into just another hunk of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 652300,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "debris."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 653300,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I should add that StarLink will be in very\nlow orbit, and so has a fast decay time - under"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 658840,
    "dDurationMs": 1430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "5 years."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 660270,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That might be enough to mitigate the dangers in this case."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 663520,
    "dDurationMs": 4890,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But StarLink isn’t going to be the last\ngiant swarm of internet satellites - in fact,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 668410,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it’s sure to inspire other companies and\nnations to launch their own."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 672210,
    "dDurationMs": 5990,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Presumably, at some point, some of them without the same care that SpaceX claims to be taking."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 678200,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "OK, let’s take the worst case scenario."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 681240,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Kessler syndrome accelerates, churning up low earth orbit into a cloud of shrapnel."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 687260,
    "dDurationMs": 2090,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What comes next?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 689350,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Some sci-fi writers like to present Kessler\nsyndrome as an impassable maelstrom, a giant"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 694780,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "space blender, effectively imprisoning us\non the Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 698360,
    "dDurationMs": 1930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That’s a bit dramatic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 700290,
    "dDurationMs": 5310,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The danger is for objects spending any lengthy period of time in those zones."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 705600,
    "dDurationMs": 5130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "For a rocket passing straight through on its way to higher obits, or to more distant parts, the"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 710730,
    "dDurationMs": 3560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "risk will probably will be tolerablely low."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 714290,
    "dDurationMs": 4870,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Higher orbits, like medium earth orbit where the GPS satellites live, will probably also"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 719160,
    "dDurationMs": 3270,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be okay due to the relative low density up\nthere."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 722430,
    "dDurationMs": 5010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Still, there are rocket boosters left over\nfrom launches to high altitudes- maybe they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 727440,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "could be destroyed in collisions in low earth orbit, creating a train of debris that wreaks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 732160,
    "dDurationMs": 1610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "havoc higher up."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 733770,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the real risk is for anything trying to\nstay in low earth orbit."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 737460,
    "dDurationMs": 3951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the late stages of the Kessler Syndrome,\nthe space below a couple of thousand km may"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 741411,
    "dDurationMs": 2959,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "be largely unusable - at least for a while."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 744370,
    "dDurationMs": 4810,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "At the very least, the cost of maintaining\na satellite presence will be prohibitively"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 749180,
    "dDurationMs": 4659,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "expensive with satellite lifetimes dropping drastically."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 753839,
    "dDurationMs": 4951,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "We’ll have to curb our appetite for global\ndigital communication for at least several"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 758790,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "years while we wait for the junk field to\nfall back to Earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 762570,
    "dDurationMs": 5380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "After about a decade, very low earth orbit\n- up to 400km - will become usable again."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 767950,
    "dDurationMs": 3380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Or we could start taking more care right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 771330,
    "dDurationMs": 5430,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s possible to plan to deorbit booster\nrockets and old satellites, or send them up"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 776760,
    "dDurationMs": 2610,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "into safer graveyard orbits."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 779370,
    "dDurationMs": 5540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And all sorts of new technology are being\ndeveloped to do this stuff, like huge deployable"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 784910,
    "dDurationMs": 6290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "sails which increase drag and cause trash\nto fall faster, or even electromagnetic tethers"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 791200,
    "dDurationMs": 3690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which push on earth’s magnetic field to\ndeorbit a satellite."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 794890,
    "dDurationMs": 6680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The key will be better organization and cooperation between nations and between companies to maintain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 801570,
    "dDurationMs": 6970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "our cosmic front yard, and continue our safe use of Earth’s orbital space time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 808540,
    "dDurationMs": 4470,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This show would be much, much harder to do without the help of the Space Time community"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 813010,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "on Patreon."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 814010,
    "dDurationMs": 3970,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Don’t worry, we’ll keep doing this no\nmatter what - but I gotta give a huge shoutout"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 817980,
    "dDurationMs": 4280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "to the Patreon crew - you guys really help\nthe show to make ends meet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 822260,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And today’s extra-extra-special shoutout\ngoes to Tiffany Poindexter, who’s supporting"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 827960,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "us at the big bang level."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 829640,
    "dDurationMs": 4220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Tiffany, we’ve used your contributions to\nfund a research program to solve the space"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 833860,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "junk problem."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 834860,
    "dDurationMs": 5400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our plan is to de-orbit all of the smaller\npieces of that shiny debris right over your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 840260,
    "dDurationMs": 4639,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "house, where they’ll burn up on reentry\nin a beautiful fireworks display in celebration"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 844899,
    "dDurationMs": 1191,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "of your awesomeness."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 846090,
    "dDurationMs": 3530,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Obviously we can’t do that for the bigger stuff because that’ll hit"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 849620,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the ground, so please let us know where you’d like us to deliver, i mean de-orbit all of that."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 854500,
    "dDurationMs": 7160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Last episode was on Planck Relics, those subatomic scale black holes that could be literally everywhere and even"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 861660,
    "dDurationMs": 1010,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "explain dark matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 862670,
    "dDurationMs": 2670,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let’s see what you guys had to say."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 865340,
    "dDurationMs": 4809,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Matt Kelly asks what happens to normal matter when it interacts with one of these tiny black"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 870149,
    "dDurationMs": 1081,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "holes."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 871230,
    "dDurationMs": 4770,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well first of all, Planck relics would be\nso impossibly tiny that all matter would be"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 876000,
    "dDurationMs": 2510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "like empty space to them."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 878510,
    "dDurationMs": 4130,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Give them any velocity at all and they stream right through matter as though it isn’t"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 882640,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "there."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 883640,
    "dDurationMs": 4630,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The gravitational interaction is weak except right next to the relic - on the scale of"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 888270,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Planck lenfths."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 889270,
    "dDurationMs": 4390,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "If you could somehow get an elementary particle like an electron within that range then perhaps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 893660,
    "dDurationMs": 2980,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it would be absorbed and the relic would start to grow."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 896640,
    "dDurationMs": 4820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The problem then is that the black hole will\nimmediately Hawking-radiate back down to a"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 901460,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Planck relic."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 902460,
    "dDurationMs": 3330,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "That will happen long before the next particle is likely to hit it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 905790,
    "dDurationMs": 5350,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Planck relics will stay Planck relics unless you can force feed them at an enormous rate."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 911140,
    "dDurationMs": 4120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Johanna Mueller never realized that the Planck mass is such a huge thing."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 915260,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I know right?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 916260,
    "dDurationMs": 5290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Two hundredths of a milligram is giant compared to the 1.6x10^-35 meters of the Planck length"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 921550,
    "dDurationMs": 3289,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "or the 5x10^-44 seconds of the Planck time."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 924839,
    "dDurationMs": 5591,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But the planck mass defines the mass of a black hole one Planck length in radius,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 930430,
    "dDurationMs": 2460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and remember, black holes are massive!"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 932890,
    "dDurationMs": 6420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Bleedingleaderq asked whether a region dense in Planck relics would emit high-energy radiation"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 939310,
    "dDurationMs": 3290,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "as the relics merged and then Hawking-radiated again"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 942600,
    "dDurationMs": 5600,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the sort of extremely cool thought that astrophysicists love because it’s something we can look"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 948200,
    "dDurationMs": 1000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 949200,
    "dDurationMs": 4829,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Unfortunately these suckers are so small that they would never, ever merge - even if they"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 954029,
    "dDurationMs": 2311,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "got within an atomic nucleus width apart."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 956340,
    "dDurationMs": 1740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They’d just fly by each other."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 958080,
    "dDurationMs": 4930,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is what makes them the perfect candidate for WIMPS - the weakly interacting massive"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 963010,
    "dDurationMs": 2720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "objects that may explain dark matter."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 965730,
    "dDurationMs": 4979,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Several of you hypothesized that there being tiny black holes everywhere perfectly explains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 970709,
    "dDurationMs": 5241,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "one of the most vexing paradoxes in the field of domestic mechanics - as in it explains"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 975950,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "what happened to your lost socks or screws or the money in your wallet."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 979500,
    "dDurationMs": 4190,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It’s also a great excuse for why you didn’t\nfinish your physics homework on time - no"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 983690,
    "dDurationMs": 5510,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "self-respecting physics professor can confidently say that a planck relic didn’t eat your"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 989200,
    "dDurationMs": 3250,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "homework. It also explains why I don’t have a funnier joke to end this episode."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 992450,
    "dDurationMs": 3550,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I swear, I wrote one down and it just vanished."
    } ]
  } ]
}
